, I didn’t connect with or care much about the characters, and the external plot took forever to kick in. Yeah they ended up together but I really didn't care about it, and didn't feel their connection or love. None of what I wish would happen happened, and – this is not the author’s fault – it wasn’t even a bit angsty, which I want and need at the moment. <br /><br />It's not a terrible book either, it just didn't do it for me, and by <i>it</i> I mean anything.<br /><br />I zoned out quite a bit at the end, and I just felt a bit meh about it all. For me, book 1 was a big positive surprise, and book 2 and 3 did not follow suit.<br /><br /><br /><b>Blanket spoiler warning ⬇️<br />⚠️ Tropes &amp; content tags ⚠️</b><br />Irish &amp; British MCs<br />Bodyguard <br />Royalty <br />Undercover detective <br />Secret hookup<br />Animosity to lovers <br />Suspense plot<br /><br /><br /><b>⚠️ Content warning ⚠️</b><br />Alcohol consumption <br />Animals hunted and killed on page by SCs (birds)<br />Themes of corruption <br />Themes of colonization<br />Mention of past parent death<br />Attacks on MCs<br />Attempted kidnapping of MC<br />Gun violence <br />References to parent with a drinking problem (past)<br />Explicit sexual content <br />Some details of slavery (slavery)<br />Violence <br />Domestic argument<br /><br /><br /><b>⚠️Book safety ⚠️</b><br /><b>Cheating:</b> No<br /><b>Other person drama:</b> MC is planning to hook up with a woman early on before anything happens between the MCs (they don’t know each other at this point), but he doesn't go through with it. They've clearly been kissing and touching when the other MC sees them but nothing beyond that. <br /><b>Breakup:</b> No<br /><b>POV:</b> 1st person, dual<br /><b>Genre:</b> Contemporary romance<br /><b>Pairing:</b> M/M<br /><b>Strict roles or versatile:</b> Don’t remember, I zoned out <br /><b>Main characters’ age:</b> 24 and not specified <br /><b>Series:</b> Interconnected series, overarching external plot