onnect with or care much about the characters, and the external plot took forever to kick in. Yeah they ended up together but I really didn't care about it, and didn't feel their connection or love. None of what I wish would happen happened, and – this is not the author’s fault – it wasn’t even a bit angsty, which I want and need at the moment. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eIt's not a terrible book either, it just didn't do it for me, and by \u003ci\u003eit\u003c/i\u003e I mean anything.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI zoned out quite a bit at the end, and I just felt a bit meh about it all. For me, book 1 was a big positive surprise, and book 2 and 3 did not follow suit.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eBlanket spoiler warning ⬇️\u003cbr /\u003e⚠️ Tropes \u0026amp; content tags ⚠️\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eIrish \u0026amp; British MCs\u003cbr /\u003eBodyguard \u003cbr /\u003eRoyalty \u003cbr /\u003eUndercover detective \u003cbr /\u003eSecret hookup\u003cbr /\u003eAnimosity to lovers \u003cbr /\u003eSuspense plot\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e⚠️ Content warning ⚠️\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAlcohol consumption \u003cbr /\u003eAnimals hunted and killed on page by SCs (birds)\u003cbr /\u003eThemes of corruption \u003cbr /\u003eThemes of colonization\u003cbr /\u003eMention of past parent death\u003cbr /\u003eAttacks on MCs\u003cbr /\u003eAttempted kidnapping of MC\u003cbr /\u003eGun violence \u003cbr /\u003eReferences to parent with a drinking problem (past)\u003cbr /\u003eExplicit sexual content \u003cbr /\u003eSome details of slavery (slavery)\u003cbr /\u003eViolence \u003cbr /\u003eDomestic argument\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e⚠️Book safety ⚠️\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eCheating:\u003c/b\u003e No\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eOther person drama:\u003c/b\u003e MC is planning to hook up with a woman early on before anything happens between the MCs (they don’t 